{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lateralus feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's intricate rhythms and atmospheric heaviness; Thirteenth Step also fits my desire for atmosphere and expressive vocals.",
    "Scream Aim Fire and Toxicity fit my heavier listening interests through melodic, fast guitar work or unpredictable rhythms, giving me something engaging beyond sheer intensity."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Way Of The Fist emphasizes blunt aggression when I am more interested in heaviness with atmosphere, melody, or intricate rhythms.",
    "Fallen and Chapter V connect with parts of my rock history, but they are weaker choices for today's mood. City of Evil, Avenged Sevenfold, and All Hope Is Gone have appeal, yet I would leave them for later while choosing my stronger matches."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My history of heavy guitar music seems to have been taken as a broad appetite for aggression, although the character of that heaviness matters to me.",
    "Albums related to my earlier rock listening seem to receive similar emphasis to albums that follow directly from my latest interest in Tool."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent choice of 10.000 Days makes intricate rhythms, atmospheric arrangements, and expressive vocals especially relevant right now.",
    "I can find an album appealing without choosing it today: melodic guitar work earns my interest, but the strongest atmospheric or rhythmically intricate choices take priority."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy music, but only some captured the atmosphere, melody, and rhythmic intricacy guiding my choices today."
}"}
